Award [2 max]
A feedback system samples the output signals (temperature) then a sample (a fraction of the
output signal) is fed back to the input;
to change/modify the input signal;
in such a way as to produce an output signal that differs substantially from the output signal
produced in the absence of such feedback / as to increase or decrease the temperature in
the house;
The output value is (continuously) compared to the desired value to produce an error value/ 
difference/ adjusting factor;  
the error value/ difference/ adjusting factor is fed to input; 
to determine the next action/ to achieve a desired outcome/pre-set temperature in the room;

